ation dispatch. This is separate\nfrom the already completed two code examinations and bounded accounting-mechanism correction.\n\n## Selected format consequence and closed schema\n\nFresh source scoping established that binary receipts change the nested value/reference semantics\nof accounting/2 evidence. Under AGENTS.md's required versioning rule, root selects explicit\naccounting/3 for this next slice. Accounting/1 and /2 readers/legacy receipt bytes, acquisition/2\nand frozen baseline bytes remain unchanged. This technical amendment does not reopen the completed\nmechanism examinations or rewrite the approved initiative snapshot.\n\nThe revised docs/design/consumer-model-behavior-native-cases.md now fixes a closed model-behavior/1\nauthority, model-behavior-execution/1 candidate/plan/executed stages, model-behavior-case/1 native\nreceipts and concrete typed accounting/3 members. Exact source/target/AST/authority/candidate/plan\nbindings, disjoint legacy/binary cases and complete claim consumption are mandatory. Duplicate raw\nJSON keys refuse before Value construction. Private execution proof cannot be deserialized.\nInitial claims require a single exact production entrypoint; diagnostic execution reports zero\nqualified cells. Actual loader cases/causal observations and root authority adoption remain owed.\n\nThe scoper returned cited/inferred source scope with high confidence and no writes/builds. Root\nselected the /3 decision during its preparation. Independent technical design review precedes\nimplementation; all complete-matrix reconciliation, aggregate and parent gate requirements remain.\n","relations":[{"specifies":"story:consumer-accounting-baseline-never-extended"}],"status":"draft","title":"Record the native execution boundary required by direct-file model cases"},"lifecycle_state":"draft"},"relations":[{"specifies":"story:consumer-accounting-baseline-never-extended"}],"title":"Record the native execution boundary required by direct-file model cases"